# Cloudflare Pages security headers (applied to every response).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://cdn.plot.ly https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://cdn.plot.ly https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self'
# ENFORCING. The host allowlists are the real protection: default-src 'self', object-src
# 'none', frame-ancestors 'none' (no clickjacking), and script/connect/frame limited to
# self + the known CDNs (jsDelivr/Plotly for the editor's Pyodide+Plotly, Turnstile,
# Supabase). script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' (the site ships several first-party inline
# scripts: analytics beacon, subscribe, Pagefind, admin reveal) and 'unsafe-eval'/
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (Pyodide) — a static site can't nonce per-request, and the injection
# surface is low (no user HTML is ever innerHTML'd unescaped). If the editor ever fails to
# load a CDN, add that host here. To debug: open devtools, watch for "Refused to…" errors.
